@Solix45456767 Hi,
1. My plugin currently supports an editor-based diff (temporary backup + `code --diff`). It handles multiple edits across multiple files reliably in my testing, but currently works only on Linux and when running opencode from the editor’s integrated terminal. You can give it a try.
2. A Webview dashboard or sidebar UI would require much larger architectural changes — likely a dedicated VS Code extension — so it’s out of scope for now, but something I may explore later.

If you use Linux + Vscode, just add this in `~/.config/opencode/opencode.jsonc`:
`
{
  "plugin": ["@hoangp8/opencode-plugin-editor-diff@0.1.0"]
}
`

@rekram1-node wanted to bring this one back: getting more info in CI when 'headless' is hugely useful to us.

right now any subagents are invisible, and any permissions errors just stall the workflows.

also applies to sandbox environments - setting `OPENCODE_EMIT_SUBAGENT_EVENTS` allows us to capture and emit those + any questions asked.
